# Build: Claude Code Session Manager (Phone → Windows Desktop)

## Context

Windows 11 desktop named `voltreezy` on Tailscale with MagicDNS enabled.
Phone reaches it at `http://voltreezy:<port>`. I'm on Claude Pro.

I use Anthropic's built-in `/remote-control` feature to drive local Claude
Code sessions from the Code tab of the Claude mobile app. That feature
works once a session is running — but it can't:

- Start a new session in a specific project folder from my phone
- Kill a stuck or context-bloated session and spin up a fresh one remotely
- Switch between projects without walking back to my desk

I need a small web-based control panel that fills exactly those gaps.
Nothing more. No terminal emulator, no chat UI — the Claude mobile app is
already both of those.

## What to build

A FastAPI service on `voltreezy` that serves a mobile-friendly web page.
The page shows registered projects as cards with Start / Restart / Stop
buttons. Tapping a button spawns, kills, or cycles a `claude` process in
the project's folder. Once a session is running, I switch to the Claude
mobile app Code tab to work with it.

## Deliverables

### 1. `session_manager/server.py`

FastAPI service with these endpoints, all behind bearer-token auth:

- `GET /` — serves the mobile web UI
- `GET /api/projects` — list projects with current session state
- `POST /api/projects/{project_id}/start` — spawn a new Claude Code
  session in that folder. If something is already running for that
  project, return an error (use /restart instead).
- `POST /api/projects/{project_id}/restart` — kill the existing session
  if any, wait 2s, spawn a fresh one.
- `POST /api/projects/{project_id}/stop` — kill the session cleanly.
- `GET /api/health` — uptime, Tailscale hostname, auth status.

**Session spawn behavior:**
- Open a new PowerShell 7 (`pwsh`) window via `subprocess.Popen` with
  `CREATE_NEW_CONSOLE` so I can see it on the desktop if needed.
- `cd` into the project folder.
- Run `claude`. Remote Control is set to auto-enable globally (see setup
  script), so no flag needed.
- Track process by PID and project_id in an in-memory dict.

**Kill behavior:**
- `taskkill /PID <pid> /T /F` to kill the process tree.
- Confirm termination before reporting success.

**Auth & binding:**
- Bearer token generated on first run, printed once, hash stored in
  `config.json`.
- Bind to the Tailscale interface only. Detect via `tailscale ip -4`.
  Do not bind to `0.0.0.0`.
- Reject requests from other interfaces.

### 2. `session_manager/web/index.html`

Single-page mobile UI. Vanilla HTML/CSS/JS, no framework.

- Dark theme. Large tap targets (min 44px). Mobile-first.
- Project cards stacked vertically, each showing:
  - Project name and folder path (truncated on small screens)
  - Status dot: green (running), gray (idle), yellow (transitioning)
  - Uptime if running ("started 15m ago")
  - Buttons: `Start` when idle, `Restart` + `Stop` when running
- After Start/Restart, show a 3s "Session starting..." state, then refresh
  status. Include hint: "Now switch to the Claude app → Code tab."
- Poll `/api/projects` every 5s.
- Auth token entered once and stored in sessionStorage. If missing or
  invalid, show token entry screen.

