## Constraints & gotchas

- **One Remote Control session per machine.** UI must enforce this:
  starting project B while project A is running requires stopping A first,
  or Restart-ing A. Make it explicit in UI copy.
- **10-minute network timeout** on Remote Control. Don't work around it —
  surface it. If tracked PID is no longer alive on the OS, mark status as
  dead and let me Restart.
- `--dangerously-skip-permissions` doesn't work with Remote Control.
  Don't pass it.
- PowerShell 7 (`pwsh`), not Windows PowerShell. Fail fast if `pwsh`
  isn't on PATH.
- Never log the auth token. Never include it in errors.

